  "published": "2026-07-20T22:46:30.173Z",
  "releaseNotes": "fix: guard the standalone DropDb against Service Broker error 8429 (\"conversation endpoint is not in a valid state for SEND ... state 'ER'\"). When SET SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE force-rolls-back a broker-enabled DB's conversations, a queued activation SEND could fail with 8429 and abort the drop. The drop batch now conditionally runs SET ERROR_BROKER_CONVERSATIONS first (no termination clause - a service_broker_option does not permit one), gated on sys.databases.is_broker_enabled = 1, so it is a no-op for every normal (broker-off) drop and never triggers 8429 for broker-enabled DBs such as ESS/NwsEnterpriseSecurity (PSDO-2845). Bumps AssemblyVersion 2026.3.01.03 -> 2026.3.01.04.",
  "repository": {
